;;; world/regions/wrongwater.map - Wrongwater's twelve rooms under the Ice
;;; Well (topics/harkfell-wrongwater-map, approved by David 2026-10-11; the
;;; six western and lower rooms G-L approved 2026-10-12, the map note's
;;; appendix). In through the drip door at the Ice Well's crack (A north);
;;; out one way east, through Against the Drip's west wall (F east). C to F
;;; and D to I are drops; L is behind a false wall in I.
(map
  region: wrongwater
  origin: (-3 7)
  layout:
  ("G-A-B-C"
   "| |   |"
   "H-D-E-F"
   "  |   |"
   "L-I-J-K")
  rooms:
  ((A "Under the Well" "you drop onto dry ground, and the water you came through hangs overhead with its surface facing down: a breath")
   (B "The Hanging Tarn" "a tarn hangs above a dry floor, and the only way higher is up through it")
   (C "The Seventh" "above the highest water, on a dry shelf, a violet note waits that no stone has ever answered")
   (D "The Upward Grove" "icicles grow up from the floor toward a lake above them, each humming faintly: a breath")
   (E "Rain Rising" "rain rises from puddles into the water overhead, and if you wait it starts to play")
   (F "The Way Out" "a passage runs east into the dark, toward a curtain of stone and a picture you may already know")
   (G "The Inverted Fall" "a column of water hangs from the roof like a waterfall stopped and turned over, and the only way to the nook above is up through it")
   (H "Stepping Lakes" "three small lakes hang at different heights, and the way up is to choose your lake and swim through it, then the next")
   (I "Under the Grove" "under the grove the icicles' roots come through the roof as pale ice, and one stretch of wall is not quite stone: a breath")
   (J "The Drowned Grove" "icicles grow up out of a dark pool under a lake that hangs over it, and you swim between them")
   (K "The Climb Back" "a rough shaft climbs from under the grove back up to the way out: a second way, and a small lake to look at on the way")
   (L "The Seventh's Rest" "behind a wall that is not quite stone, a still pool hangs over a dry floor and a picture shows the note that is wrong and belongs: a breath"))
  borders: ((A north) (F east)))
